{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Remove the duplicate module-level `_load`/`_kinds`/`guard` definitions (lines 55-67) in test_collection_isolation_guard.py; keep a single copy.","criteria":["maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py:36 `def _load():` (first definition)","tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py:44 `guard = _load()` (first)","tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py:55 `def _load():` (identical redefinition)","tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py:63 `guard = _load()` (second)","tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py:47-52 define `_findings`/`_kinds`, then `_kinds` is redefined at 66-67"],"finding":"The oracle test file redefines module-level helpers `_load`, `_kinds`, and the `guard` module object twice (lines 36-44 and again 55-63; `_kinds` at 51-52 and 66-67). The second block re-executes the module and shadows the first — dead, duplicated code that is confusing and can mask divergence if only one copy is edited.","id":"0","impact":0.3,"location":"tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py:55","norm_id":"nbb8ebea5fd9a2940","priority":0.3,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"suggested_fix":"Delete the second `_load`/`guard`/`_kinds` block (lines 55-67); the first block already binds all three.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":true,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make `_check_home_escape` consult harness provenance (skip when the argv element also mentions `tmp_path`/a fixture param) so a harness-owned path named `home` is not falsely failed.","criteria":["correctness","edge-cases"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/_subprocess_isolation.py:56 `_HOME_ESCAPE_NAMES = frozenset({\"home\", \"mkdtemp\", \"TemporaryDirectory\"})`","tests/_subprocess_isolation.py:303-306 `names = _referenced_names(element)` then `if not (names & _HOME_ESCAPE_NAMES ...)` — no `harness`/`tmp_path` guard, unlike `_check_root` which excuses `_mentions(explicit, harness)`","tests/unit/test_harness_shims.py:49 `home = tmp_path / \"home\"` shows a real harness-owned variable named `home`","_check_home_escape is not passed the `harness` set, so it cannot distinguish `tmp_path`-derived paths"],"finding":"`_check_home_escape` flags a spawn as a hazard whenever any argv element references a name/attribute in `_HOME_ESCAPE_NAMES` (`home`, `mkdtemp`, `TemporaryDirectory`), without consulting whether that path is harness-owned. A harness-provided path bound to a variable literally named `home` (e.g. `home = tmp_path / \"home\"` — the exact idiom used in the modified test_harness_shims.py) passed positionally in argv would be reported as a hazard and FAIL collection, a false positive in the collection-failing direction.","id":"1","impact":0.27,"location":"tests/_subprocess_isolation.py:302","norm_id":"nb9d5370eb3f173da","priority":0.1736,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"suggested_fix":"Pass `harness` into `_check_home_escape` and `continue` when `_mentions(element, harness)` is true, mirroring the accept path in `_check_root`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":true,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":true,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test that drives a real hazar